  "id": "65b1f595-4262-5a17-bf03-5a87adc13e1d",
  "slug": "gingersnap-strips",
  "name": "Gingersnap Strips",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "I have been making these spicy cookies for about 30 years, and they are always a hit! I have tweaked the recipe over the years, and they are truly addictive!",
  "cuisine": null,
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Line two cookie sheets with parchment paper, or you may use ungreased cookie sheets."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "In a medium bowl, cream together the shortening and sugar until smooth. Beat in the egg and molasses. Combine the flour, baking soda, salt, cinnamon, ginger and cloves; stir into the batter until it forms a dough. The dough may seem a bit crumbly, but that is ok. Keep mixing and it will come together."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Remove dough from the bowl, and knead for a few turns. Pat out into a square, and divide into 6 equal pieces. Roll each piece out into a 12 inch long log. Place 3 logs onto each cookie sheet. Wet the tops of the logs with a little bit of water using your fingertips, then sprinkle with sugar."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Bake for 10 to 12 minutes in the preheated oven. Allow the cookies to cool for a couple of minutes, then slice the bars diagonally into 1 inch pieces using a knife or pizza cutter. Remove from cookie sheets to cool on wire racks. When completely cool, store in an airtight container at room temperature."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 60,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 12,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 20,
